art.\n   - We also know: "If Charlie is not young then Charlie is smart.".\n   - Since Charlie is big, he could be young or not young.\n   - If Charlie is not young, he is smart.\n   - If Charlie is young, he is not smart.\n\n3. **Charlie\'s color:**.\n   - From the context: "All blue things are young.".\n   - Since Charlie is blue, he must be young.\n   - We also know: "If Charlie is young and Charlie is blue then Charlie is not smart.".\n   - Since Charlie is young and blue, he is not smart.\n   - We also know: "If Charlie is big and Charlie is young then Charlie is not smart.".\n   - Since Charlie is big and young, he is not smart.\n   - Therefore, Charlie is not smart.\n\n4. **Charlie\'s shape and smartness:**.\n   - Since Charlie is not smart, he cannot be round (as round things are big and big, young things are smart).\n   - Therefore, Charlie is not round.\n   - Since Charlie is big and young, he must be white (as all blue things are young and round things are big, so white must be the remaining color for big, young things).\n\n5. **Conclusion:**.\n   - Charlie is not white because he is not round. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
